  "summary": "This study compared a simplified pressure-controlled initial reperfusion technique (group II, n=37) to standard technique (group I, n=20) in patients undergoing emergent CABG after acute MI, finding that the innovative technique resulted in higher spontaneous sinus rhythm recurrence (86% vs 45%), lower postoperative myocardial infarction (1 vs 5), and lower enzyme levels, suggesting effectiveness in preventing ischemia-reperfusion injury."
